00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.540
Episode 11: Takamatsu Festival

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.550
If that's the case, I could manage 
to work and still take care of him...

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.120
Poco?!

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:42.890
Huh?!

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.140
What happened?

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.400
Ribbit, ribbit.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:53.400
Huh?

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.270
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.590
Whoa!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.180
I'll have to get serious about 
disciplining him and such, too...

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:05.080
Huh?

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.670
Souta.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.570
Yeah.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:20.720
Rin!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.050
That's right.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.410
<b>Kindergarten 
Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.320
<b>Entrance 
Ceremony</b>

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.430
Oh... I was this age when Mom...

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.110
Souta?

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:51.140
Nostalgic, isn't it?

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.580
Nostalgic!

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:04.530
<i>I hated Kagawa at that time.</i>

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.400
<i>There were mountains everywhere you looked,</i>

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:13.100
<i>and not even the kind that felt majestic at all.</i>

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:23.250
<i>As our house got closer, 
you could smell the udon stock.</i>

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.590
<i>I'd take the long way home to get 
there after the restaurant closed.</i>

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.460
<i>I hated living like that every day.</i>

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.700
I wonder why it is...

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.790
I remember so much when I'm with you, Poco.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.190
What this?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.190
That's cotton candy.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.550
Cotton candy!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.680
<b>Udon</b>

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.200
<i>When I was little,</i>

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.430
<i>I loved watching Dad make udon.</i>

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.390
<i>Back then, I always assumed</i>

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.930
<i>I'd grow up to make udon, too.</i>

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.810
<i>But at some point, I stopped wanting 
to take over the restaurant.</i>

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.570
<i>That said, I didn't find anything else 
I particularly wanted to do.</i>

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.450
<i>If I'd never met Dahama-san,</i>

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.620
<i>maybe I'd have gone on like that forever.</i>

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.890
<i>I should have talked with Dad more.</i>

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.960
I've been like this ever since we came back.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.280
We'll have to make a photo album for you, too.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.390
Poco, look this way.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.720
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:30.840
Huh?

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.600
Yow!

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:35.810
Hey!

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:44.600
Ah! That was the last shot on that roll of film...

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.240
<i>Gao!</i>

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:53.700
<b>51st Kagawa 
Takamatsu Festival</b>

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.900
<i>The Takamatsu Festival...</i>

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:51.430
<i>...is almost here!</i>

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:53.700
<i>Gao.</i>

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.690
<i>Let's sing and dance...</i>

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.170
<i>...and have fun!</i>

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.210
<i>Gao!</i>

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.830
Gao!

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.660
It's that time of year already?

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:05.460
<b>Team Planet 
Saeki Manabu
Incoming Call</b>

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.460
Manabu-san?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.040
Hello, Tawara speaking.

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:09.800
Yes. Yes.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:11.470
A job?!

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.650
Of course!

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:14.350
Absolutely! Thank you!

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:16.340
Okay, I'll see you then.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:17.370
Goodbye.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.040
Poco, we're going to go see Gaogao-chan.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.730
<b>Kagawa 
Takamatsu 
Festival</b>

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.990
<b>Smile Ball</b>

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.990
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.990
<b>Grilled Squid</b>

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.990
<b>Takamatsu Festival</b>

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.870
What a cute little girl.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.670
He's a boy, actually.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.300
What?!

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.160
Manabe-san, thank you.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.630
Poco's over the moon.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:50.130
Oh, I should be thanking you for 
lending a hand. It's a big help.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:54.010
Thanks to you, we'll be able to 
stream the festival in real time.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.610
I can get started today!

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:00.140
Great. We really are shorthanded.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.860
Gaogao!

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:06.690
Actually, I have Yukie inside that costume.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.280
Huh?

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.280
She may not look it, 
but she's a Shaolin black belt.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.210
She's scary when she's mad, but she's tough!

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.290
<i>Manabu-san, you're the scariest of all.</i>

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.340
Good work.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.870
Thank you. It's so hot, I'm completely parched.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:33.430
The day of the festival is going to be brutal!

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.260
But, Yukie-san, you seem like you're enjoying this.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.550
It makes me happy when clients

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.180
appreciate and enjoy our work.

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:48.280
That's why I do this job.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.160
I learned how that felt 
after meeting Dahama-san.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:00.970
That was why I decided to 
do Web design in Tokyo

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:02.690
and left Kagawa.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.270
Oh, is that why?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.780
But now I know that I can

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:09.420
keep doing this job, even out here.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.170
All thanks to you and Manabe-san.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.460
Well, our journey here took some

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.130
twists and turns, too.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.560
Ask Dahama-kun about it sometime.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:23.630
I will. I'm glad

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.310
I met Dahama-san that summer.

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.960
He's the one who introduced you to Manabu, too.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.190
It really is all thanks to Dahama-kun.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:33.640
Yes.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:46.860
<i>I wish</i>

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.100
<i>I'd had a real talk with Dad.</i>

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:54.720
<i>I wish I'd told him that I found 
something I truly wanted to do.</i>

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:04.790
Gao!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.480
<b>Kagawa 
Takamatsuri 
Festival</b>

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.480
<b>51st Kagawa Takamatsu Festival</b>

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:06.480
<b>Come check us out! 
"Terrific Takamatsu"</b>

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.480
This is a great site.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.860
I can hardly believe I'm involved in 
this kind of work, even in Kagawa.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.110
Gao!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:15.110
Poco, you've been a tanuki a lot lately, 
even when you're not sleeping, huh?

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:20.530
Is it tiring to be human all 
the time, even in Kagawa?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.120
It's from Manabe-san.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:32.130
<b>Manabe-san</b>

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:32.130
<b>Thank you so much!
I'll call you if I need anything else.

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.470
<i>Are you going to the Takamatsu Festival?</i>

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.730
<i>They're selling jinbei cheap.</i>

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.730
<i>Want me to buy some for you two?</i>

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:33.680
I'd really appreciate that.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:36.190
Mom friends are just what you need.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.130
<b>Former First Love</b>

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:39.510
Hot...

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.850
I'll take a beer.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.250
Didn't you drive here?

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.180
I'll stay overnight. It's cool.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.390
You're staying overnight?!

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.740
One, two, udon, udon.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:53.420
One, two. Souta, too!

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.530
One, two!

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.740
Yeah, I'm coming.

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:00.590
One, two, udon, udon.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.720
One, two, udon, udon.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.000
One, two, udon, udon.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.670
What's this? Did ya decide 
to take over the restaurant?

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:08.640
Well,

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.420
I do think I'm able to make it 
taste pretty good now, but...

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:16.420
Then you oughta do it. 
I'll come by to eat every day.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.890
Actually, I plan to keep doing

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:21.120
Web-related work from here,

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.180
although I'll be a freelancer for a while.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.810
What? So you're just a freeter?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.040
Not a freeter! A freelancer!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:29.570
Same thing, ain't it?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:30.710
No, it's not!

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:34.320
You'd better apologize to all the 
freelancers and freeters in the country!

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:35.440
Not my problem.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:36.870
But...

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.790
I found something I want to do here.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.380
I think I'll be able to support Poco, too.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:45.950
Well, give it your best shot.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:48.210
I'll be comin' by to eat lunch.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:51.960
I told you, I'm not going to 
start an udon restaurant!

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.940
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:10:58.230 --> 00:10:59.910
Poco-chan, is it good?

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:01.470
Yummy, yummy!

00:11:01.730 --> 00:11:04.580
Good thing I bought a big one.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:08.480
Sis, you didn't run away from 
home or something, did you?

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.370
Now, why would ya think that?

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.030
My husband's in Tokyo on a 
business trip for a little while.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:14.630
There's the Takamatsu Festival, too.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.390
I came home for it. That's all.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:17.740
Not to mention...

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.040
Sis.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:22.990
Hmm?

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.550
About Poco...

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.900
I've decided to raise him.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:28.500
Really?

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.270
Yeah.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.320
What about Poco-chan? Is he all right 
with it? Did you explain it to him?

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.000
I'm going to talk to him soon.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.260
What did his parents say?

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.320
I dunno... Now that I know 
I'm gonna be a parent myself,

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.560
I get stuck on all sorts of things.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:52.050
Poco... isn't actually a friend's child.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:54.530
Huh? Then what is he?

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:55.850
Poco's...

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:58.800
Whose is he?

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.470
Listen...

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.390
When we visited Mom's grave,

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.660
did ya see anything strange?

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:17.770
It was like a vision, but it was so real.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.530
Like we'd gone back into the past.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.890
You saw it, too, didn't ya?

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:25.010
What was that?

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.440
Does it have somethin' to do with Poco-chan?

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.710
I don't know, either.

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.980
Hey, Rinko. You're here?

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:37.410
Y-Yeah.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.160
What are you doin' here so late?

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.820
Had a night shift.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.030
Did ya come by for the festival?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.530
Yeah. Are you goin' to the 
Takamatsu Festival, too?

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:50.500
Yeah, think I will. It's been a while.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.700
Cotton candy!

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.470
I'll buy you some.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.290
Let's all go to the festival together.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.450
But Shinobu-chan,

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.830
don't ya have somebody else to go with?

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.070
What're you goin' on about?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.180
Your marriage interview. How'd it go?

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:07.810
Oh, I gave it to her straight.

00:13:07.810 --> 00:13:10.000
Told her I wanna focus on my career for now,

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.810
so I'm not lookin' to get married, and 
to please turn me down from her end.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.200
What a thing to say!

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.860
It was true.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:19.010
Then she said,

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:21.010
"Thank God."

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.620
Want more watermelon?

00:13:25.620 --> 00:13:26.770
Yeah!

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:28.160
I'll cut you some.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:36.210
<b>Takamatsu Festival</b>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.210
<b>Smile Ball</b>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.210
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.210
<b>Fried Squid</b>

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.800
Isn't my yukata cute?

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:43.960
Cute.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.740
Manabe-san, you're a lifesaver. Thanks for this.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.930
Mom friends have to look out for each other.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.810
Okay, Poco. Shall we go 
buy that cotton candy?

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.680
We'll be back.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.270
They really look like father and son.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.110
How long's Poco-chan gonna be in Kagawa?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.400
I wonder...

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:16.620
Yo.

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:19.360
Heard you're streaming the festival?

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.780
Senpai, how mean!

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.750
How could you not invite us to the festival?

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.230
Dahama-san! And Hiroshi, too?

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.390
Good evening to everyone here 
at the Tamakatsu Festival.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.800
I'm your host, Okuda Mai.

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:35.890
In just a moment, the opening ceremony 
will be taking place on the main stage.

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.230
Thanks to Souta-kun,

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.860
our Web commercial made 
a tremendous impact, too.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.320
Oh, is that so?

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.010
My people were very happy about it, too.

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:49.950
They said the number of views 
spiked up dramatically.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.730
I'm happy that

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:54.940
it was so well-received.

00:14:58.570 --> 00:15:01.580
Poco-chan, your mouth's all sticky.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.600
Nozomi, you noticed?

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.170
'Cuz I'm a big sister!

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:10.090
Poco-chan, your mom and dad 
aren't coming to the festival?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:12.720
Aren't you lonely?

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.640
You're not lonely, right?

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.110
Yeah!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:21.880
Souta, Rin, Nozomi,

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.360
Granny... Nakaji!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.860
I'm last?

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.860
That's right. It's not lonely at all, is it?

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:34.370
Souta and Poco-chan might 
get to stay together forever.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:36.690
It looks like that's what Souta wants, too.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.080
Well, here we are in Kagawa Prefecture!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.500
That's right.

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.810
Senpai! Little guy!

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:48.330
Hii-kun!

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:51.010
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.890
<b>Masks 
100 yen</b>

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.390
<i>Back then,</i>

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:00.270
<i>Dad would carry me on his 
shoulders like this, too.</i>

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:04.520
<i>Being with Poco brings 
back so many memories.</i>

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.910
So, how long is Poco-chan gonna be here?

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:15.050
Nozomi was askin'.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:17.910
Forever, maybe.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.500
Oh, really?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.460
Yeah. I decided to adopt him.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:23.710
Did ya?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.600
Right... Maybe that's a good idea.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:31.020
You and Poco-chan look like

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.050
a real family to me.

00:16:34.730 --> 00:16:35.430
You know...

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.060
I've started to feel like that, too.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.190
The big dance is about to start.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.710
Gao!

00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.940
Everyone!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.070
It's time to dance!

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.910
Looks like they're having fun.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.460
That's a great smile...

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:12.050
Tawara-san!

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:14.630
Evening.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.570
Hello.

00:17:15.570 --> 00:17:17.590
Oh, hello. Good evening.

00:17:17.850 --> 00:17:19.990
Still here in Kagawa?

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.600
Any plans for the udon restaurant?

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:25.740
I haven't reopened it.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.200
But I'm experimenting with my dad's recipes.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.570
If you like, you can come by 
and taste-test it sometime.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.990
Can I?!

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.380
Although I can't guarantee you'll enjoy it...

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:35.870
I'm dying to eat it.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.510
Yes, please.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.370
<b>Gurgle   Rumble</b>

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:42.160
Talking about udon's got me hungry...

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.050
I'm going to go buy something.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:48.630
So sorry that she always goes on about udon.

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:52.700
The udon at Tawara-san's 
restaurant truly was the best.

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.130
She still says that, even now.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.400
I'm grateful that

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:59.380
there's someone who remembers 
the taste of my dad's udon.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.270
So pretty!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.830
Wow! They're doing fireworks, huh?

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:10.990
Uh-huh. It's the climax of the festival.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:14.810
Poco, those are called "fireworks."

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.340
Fireworks.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.220
<b>Takamatsu Festival</b>

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.480
They're beautiful...

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:25.800
Yes, so beautiful...

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.000
Who the heck are you?

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.390
That kid has a tail!

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:48.420
A tail!

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.020
It's a tail!

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:51.920
A tail! A tail!

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:56.520
We got this at the shooting booth. 
Poco wanted to put it on...

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.820
Oh, really?

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:59.450
He looks like a tanuki.

00:19:14.990 --> 00:19:16.100
<i>This is bad...</i>

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:53.020
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:53.020
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.240
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan and</i>

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:59.020
<b>Episode 11: "Gaogao-chan 
and The Bond of Friendship"</b>

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:58.290
<i>The Bond of Friendship!</i>

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:01.320
<i>Scaredy Cat-san found the courage</i>

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.970
<i>to drive a car,</i>

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.780
<i>and crashed into the repair workshop.</i>

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:10.290
<i>W-We can't fix this...</i>

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.310
<i>I'm fine.</i>

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.680
<i>Look! I made it out, fit as a fiddle!</i>

00:21:14.680 --> 00:21:17.420
<i>Talk about a lucky break, huh?</i>

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.130
<i>Momo-chan?</i>

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.640
<i>That workshop...</i>

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:25.890
<i>We made so many great memories there...</i>

00:21:25.890 --> 00:21:27.700
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.850
<i>Dry your eyes.</i>

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.130
<i>Your mascara is running, gao.</i>

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.560
<i>We'll all work together 
to fix the workshop, gao!</i>

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.630
<i>I want to fix it,</i>

00:21:37.630 --> 00:21:40.320
<i>but all this rubble is too heavy for us...</i>

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:42.820
<i>Gao!</i>

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:44.820
<i>Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.590
<i>And so, Mimi and Momo</i>

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:50.580
<i>started to rebuild their 
broken repair workshop.</i>

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:52.730
<i>We can do it if we try, gao!</i>

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:53.450
<i>Let's have lunch!</i>

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:55.100
<i>It'll be okay.</i>

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.470
<i>As long as we're with Gaogao-chan, 
we can fix anything.</i>

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:07.260
Hey, what's this character's name?

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:10.160
Hmm, his name is...

00:22:10.160 --> 00:22:11.670
Gaogao-chan.

00:22:11.670 --> 00:22:14.680
His backstory is that he came 
from the edge of outer space.

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:16.270
"Gaogao-chan"?

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:20.110
He's a hard romanticist like you, Dahama.

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:21.170
Yeah, right.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:22.170
I've got it!

00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:29.740
His friends, Mimi and Momo.

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:32.470
He'd be lonely all by himself, right?

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:35.950
<b>The End</b>

